    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1954578202191688171",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1954578202191688171",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1954578202191688171",
      "text": "[5:14PM] #VI #Lekki #TrafficUpdate \n\nTraffic from McWen Bridge, both inward and outward Bonny Camp Roundabout, is smooth at this time. Movement along Ahmadu Bello Way in both directions, en route to Eko Hotel and back, is also good. From Bonny Camp Underbridge through Kofo Abayomi, Oniru Kilimanjaro, and down to the Ozumba stretch, traffic is good in both directions, with only minor delays caused by traffic light intervals and necessary alternations.\n\nInward Law School, towards Adeyemo Alakija, is experiencing slow movement due to an ongoing event at Muri Okunola Park, with traffic officers on ground managing the situation. The stretch from Law School to Civic Center, BJ 1004, School Corner, and onward to Sandfield in the direction of Lekki Phase 1 and return, is moving steadily, with slight holdups at alternation points. \n\nAt present, no impediments have been sighted along the major expressways. Our officers are visibly on ground ensuring smooth vehicular movement. \n\n#FollowLASTMA",
